  "content": "<b>Meaning/Usage</b>: To ask someone to stop what they are doing.\n<b>Explanation</b>: This is a common way of telling a person to stop something that is bothering you. It is more aggressive way of say, \"please dont do that.\"\n\"Please <b>stop it</b>! You're giving me a headache.\"\n\"<b>Stop</b> it before you get hurt!\"\n\"You had better <b>stop it</b> or you will get in trouble!\"\n<b>A.</b> \"Tommy! <b>Stop it</b> right now!\"\n<b>B.</b> \"Why? I saw other kids doing it.\"\n<b>A.</b> \"That's not how we behave in a restaurant.\"\n<b>B.</b> \"OK, I'm sorry.\"\nOther Common Sentences\n\"Quit what you are doing.\"\n\"Don't do that!\"",
